  "notes": "{蔓延|まんえん} uses the kanji {蔓|つる} (vine), creating an image of something spreading like creeping vines that are hard to contain.\n\nUsage:\n- {蔓延|まんえん}する (to spread, become rampant)\n- {蔓延|まんえん}を{防|ふせ}ぐ (to prevent the spread)\n- {蔓延|まんえん}{防止|ぼうし} (prevention of spread)\n\nCommonly used with:\n- {感染症|かんせんしょう}/{病気|びょうき} (infectious diseases/illness)\n- {汚職|おしょく}/{腐敗|ふはい} (corruption)\n- {犯罪|はんざい} (crime)\n- {悪習|あくしゅう} (bad habits)\n\nNote: Almost always used for negative things that spread undesirably.\n\nRelated words:\n- {拡散|かくさん}する: to spread, diffuse\n- {流行|りゅうこう}する: to be popular, epidemic\n- {横行|おうこう}する: to be rampant, run wild",
